# Contributing rule packs

Shared rules are Cursor plugins. Do not put rules meant for other people only in `.cursor/rules/`. That folder applies to this repository.

When asked to add a rule for other Cursor users:

1. Copy `templates/rule-plugin` to `plugins/<kebab-name>/`.
2. Set `name` in `plugins/<kebab-name>/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` to that folder name.
3. Write one `.mdc` per concern, under 50 lines, with a BAD/GOOD example. Leave `alwaysApply` false unless every installed project needs it on every chat. Keep the description under 200 characters.
4. Add an original `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` only when a rule is the wrong shape. Match `name` to the folder. At most two skills may omit `disable-model-invocation: true`. Do not paste an upstream skill; check `catalog/skills.json` first.
5. Add a matching entry to `.cursor-plugin/marketplace.json`. Use the same description as `plugin.json`.
6. Run `python3 scripts/validate_plugins.py`.

Choose when the rule applies:

- Relevant by description: `alwaysApply: false` and a `description`, no `globs`.
- Specific files: `alwaysApply: false`, `globs`, and a `description`.
- Every chat: `alwaysApply: true` only when the rule is safe for every project that installs the pack.
- Manual: `alwaysApply: false` and no `description` or `globs`, so it loads only when @-mentioned.

Do not put secrets, credentials, or project-private paths in a shared rule.
